/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/skill-project-management/.task-board/EPIC-260725-2h5434_session-manager-hardening-backlog/STORY-260725-s3cdji_goal-v2-compat-and-recovery-hardening/TASK-260730-2c1e8l_require-negative-tests-for-gates/progress.md:79:spawn selection rationale tuple: {"role":"reviewer","pair":"gpt-5.6-sol/high","text":"Cycle-2 review against your own F1, and note the irony worth checking carefully: this task encodes the rule that a check the production path never reaches counts as absent, and you found the encoding itself missing from the lite profile because the lite template omits RoleBody. Verify both halves of the fix. First, that a lite reviewer now actually receives the required clauses — the licence to attempt to defeat a gate, the licence to reject positive-path-only evidence, and the instruction to grep for production callers — by composing the prompt the way template.go composes it for the lite profile and reading what comes out, not by reading the template source. Condensed wording is acceptable, absence is not. Second, that the new test drives the COMPOSED production path rather than asserting the raw template and the role body separately, which is precisely how this hid. The producer was also asked to check whether developer, tester or orchestrator clauses live only in RoleBody and are therefore equally absent under lite; do not take that survey on trust, compose a lite prompt for one of those roles yourself and look. Confirm the byte budget and contract-phrase tests were kept honest rather than loosened, and that make test and make vet are green. If the criteria are met, say so plainly."}
