/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/.temp/TASK-260728-2u5u14/reviewer-gen1-DlaH9Z/decisions/0002-canonical-json-and-registry-trust.md:26:- RFC 8785 was rejected for schema 1 because its numeric and string rules would
/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/skill-project-management/.task-board/EPIC-260720-1fjsu9_board-workflow-and-spawn-policy-enhancements/STORY-260721-3er9sm_per-story-worktree-isolation-for-spawn/TASK-260803-323q82_implement-change-request-review-and-rework/progress.md:51:spawn selection rationale tuple: {"role":"reviewer","pair":"claude-opus-5","text":"First review of the ChangeRequest MR-equivalent contract. Read TASK-260803-323q82_results.md, then .research/260721_worktree-isolation-and-integration.md sections 4, 5, 5.1, 9.1 and gaps C and H as the contract. This is a large first delivery - a new internal/changerequest package plus nine named production integration points - so budget your attack rather than spreading it thin. Context that should shape where you look: this task's immediate predecessor on the same story, TASK-260803-23mz3h, was accepted after seven review cycles in which every single finding was one shape - a failed read reported as an absence, a rule asserted in a comment with no test behind it, or a gate computed correctly and then discarded by its only consumer. Hunt that shape first here. The producer clearly knew it was coming and named a git rev-parse that distinguishes absent from could-not-ask, so verify that distinction is real at every classification site rather than only at the one it advertises. Five design decisions are stated and each is an argument that deserves attacking rather than accepting. ONE, accept_cr writes status first and CR second, justified by claiming the reverse order would leave an accepted CR whose element never left reviewing while the chosen order leaves a recoverable to-review with no accepted CR because such a reviewer run is cancelled and respawned - verify that recovery actually happens rather than being asserted, because the whole ordering argument rests on it. TWO, the CR base is the branch tip at completion rather than the provisioning OID, on the grounds that measuring against provisioning would make a later leaf silently revert earlier checkpointed leaves - construct that multi-leaf scenario and confirm. THREE, the board-path rule is segment-aware rather than a string prefix so real files named .task-boardish or .task-board-notes.md survive - test both. FOUR, drift compares tree OID AND patch digest, with the claim that a tree-only check admits a candidate whose recorded patch no longer matches - narrow it to each half alone and see if a test dies for each. FIVE, the lite template omits RoleBody, which is why the consistency assertion exists - break one surface at a time and confirm each is caught. Two honesty notes to judge on merit rather than reward for disclosure. The producer reports its failed-read row needed a second pass because the first version asserted only cancelled and respawned, which the swallowing mutant ALSO produces by falling through to the status switch, so the row now asserts the recorded reason as the only discriminating observable - re-narrow that gate yourself and confirm the current row genuinely discriminates. The producer also reports finding and fixing a test-validity defect in inherited helpers, where goalLifecycleTestActions double keys its board lookup to the literal TASK-A so every evidence check failed for the wrong reason and rejection rows passed without their gate ever refusing - verify the override fixes it rather than masking something else, and check whether that same inherited defect silently weakens OTHER existing suites that still use the unoverridden helper, because if it does that is a finding larger than this task. The producer claims all snapshot, checkpoint and drift behaviour runs against real Git repositories and real linked worktrees with no fake runner, on the reasoning that a fake agreeing with the implementation about what git add -A stages proves nothing - confirm no fake crept in. Attribution you can rely on but should spot-check: the full cmd suite is red on TestRunSpawnAppliesCeilingAndAuditsCodexAndClaude due to SeedClass, SpreadGroup and LimitDegradation audit fields from the concurrent rate-limit work, and cmd/spawn_runtime.go is gofmt-dirty from that same agent and was deliberately left alone; another agent is editing cmd/ RIGHT NOW so expect churn and scope your attribution to this task files. pkg/board is red at clean HEAD on BUG-260806-u090lv. Use -count=1 for every gate you cite, per BUG-260806-i4508l. Do not supply commit_ack. Run gates in the FOREGROUND and say plainly whether the criteria are met."}
