ion audit fields from the concurrent rate-limit work, and cmd/spawn_runtime.go is gofmt-dirty from that same agent and was deliberately left alone; another agent is editing cmd/ RIGHT NOW so expect churn and scope your attribution to this task files. pkg/board is red at clean HEAD on BUG-260806-u090lv. Use -count=1 for every gate you cite, per BUG-260806-i4508l. Do not supply commit_ack. Run gates in the FOREGROUND and say plainly whether the criteria are met.
/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/skill-project-management/.task-board/EPIC-260720-1fjsu9_board-workflow-and-spawn-policy-enhancements/STORY-260721-3er9sm_per-story-worktree-isolation-for-spawn/TASK-260803-23mz3h_implement-store-board-write-journal-and-rendering-probe/progress.md:170:Cycle 6 rework. Both cycle-5 findings were missing bounds, not defects, so this cycle adds three test rows and one helper and changes NO production code. F1: added TestOwnsRefusesUnownedAtEveryPostLoadSiteUnderAFault with two rows that reach the directory-mismatch and undeclared-resource unowned sites by faulting an UNRELATED second epic, so the element under test still loads instead of terminating at elem == nil. Each row asserts the walk reported a fault AND that FindByID still resolves the element, so a row cannot silently degrade back into a duplicate of the first site coverage - that missing guard is what produced the finding. Reviewer payload2probe scaffolding not carried over. F2: added a third row to TestStagedPathOutsideTheControlRootIsRefused for staged_path == .. driven through the real store.RecoverPendingMutations entry point, not the helper. Mutation matrix: 5 mutants, 5 killed, 0 survivors, every one a NARROWING in place rather than a deletion, run in an isolated .temp repo copy so the shared working tree was never mutated. M-B and M-C now die only by the new test, which confirms the delivered suite genuinely did not cover those sites. M-G2 is the paired direction proving the two confineToControlRoot clauses cover different paths. Notable: under M-G recovery did not merely mis-classify, it reached os.Remove ON THE CONTROL ROOT PARENT DIRECTORY and failed only because that directory was non-empty - the site is destructively live. Gates for this slice all exit 0: go build, go vet, go test ./internal/store/ -count=1, go test ./... -count=1 on tools/board-cli, and pkg/board/resourcefs ok. make vet 0. IMPORTANT gate correction, and the cycle-5 verdict asked for a re-run: make test now reports exit 0 but that number is FALSE - the Makefile test targets omit -count=1 and the log shows pkg/board served (cached). With GOFLAGS=-count=1 make test is exit 2. Recorded as a gate defect, flagged not fixed, outside this slice. Attribution verified in a clean detached HEAD worktree rather than asserted: pkg/board two context-registry tests DO reproduce at clean HEAD and their files are unmodified and absent from this diff, confirming the verdict; pkg/remoteconfig is GREEN at clean HEAD and red only in the working tree from the concurrent spawn-limits slice, which this task touches no file of. make regress red, exit 2, 12 pass 11 fail, same set as cycle 5, BUG-260804-l1ey25. Re-verified the load-bearing unobtainable-baseline claim myself: HEAD does not compile board-cli. Characterised it further and flagged for the orchestrator - commit 08df995 landed the CALLERS while StagePayload and DiscardStagedPayload were never committed and exist only in this slice uncommitted pkg/board/resourcefs/delete.go, so delete.go must land with or before those callers or HEAD stays unbuildable. No code change needed, working tree is correct and builds. Scope unchanged: no admission, no CAS, no manifest membership, no withdrawn surfaces. Cycle-5 work confirmed by the reviewer was not reopened.
