/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/skill-project-management/.task-board/EPIC-260721-39av2o_agentic-system-broker-model-layering/STORY-260828-262l81_task-aware-spawn-model-recommendations/TASK-260828-3vluw7_design-workload-class-recommendation-contract/progress.md:140:Revision 6 published, resolving all 4 findings in the cycle-5 review verdict (CR-TASK-260828-3vluw7-5, revision 5): (1) advisory:true/auto_select:false now scoped to shape 3 only (configured:true, class_resolved:true) — shapes 1/2 correctly omit them, no payload changed, only the contradicting prose line fixed; (2) explicit-override accompanying task_class is now uniformly discarded (not echoed) — the response/digest/rationale-tuple were already consistent under discard, only the outlier precedence-rule sentence was fixed; (3) invalid --workload-class against an unconfigured section now deterministically refuses with recommendation_confirmation_not_allowed (configured-gate checked before enum validation), matching the existing configured-first pattern already used for rationale/digest/transport; (4) SS15 agent instructions now require task_class=CLASS or workload_class=OVERRIDE on the preflight call before reading recommendations/available_pairs, and carry the same source through to the matching spawn-time flag. Added SS11 cases 19-20 as dedicated negative tests, SS21 as the cycle-5 decision log. No prior accepted decision reopened: no payload shape, digest input, filtering rule, or admission scope changed from revision 5. Spec-only change (no Go code touched); go vet and the reviewer-cited targeted tests (TestResolveSelection_NoCeilingPreservesCurrentSelections, TestModelsForAgent_Claude, TestValidateSpawnReasoningEffort_Claude) all pass, and the code line citations underpinning the design (pkg/board/types.go:95-98, role.go:109-147) were spot-checked against current source. Left uncommitted for the CR-6 snapshot. Not self-accepting; routed to independent review.
