   124	
   125	## Canonical JSON and Immutable Object Identities
   126	
   127	[`internal/canonicaljson`](internal/canonicaljson) exposes the production RFC
   128	8785 JCS entry point and the AX immutable-object identity calculation. The JCS
   129	path validates I-JSON input before canonicalization, including duplicate-name,
   130	UTF-8, surrogate-pair, ECMAScript number-formatting, string-escaping, and
   131	UTF-16 property-ordering rules. Its number behavior is checked against every
   132	finite RFC 8785 Appendix B sample through the production entry point.
   133	
   134	The AX identity path additionally enforces the Section 1.6 common model: JSON
   135	numbers are integral safe integers, and the exact `schema`/`schema_version`
   136	pair selects the schema-defined self field from the pinned v0.5.0 identity
   137	contract. Other registered ID names may remain as ordinary references; only
   138	the selected schema's own field is removed before JCS and SHA-256. Callers
   139	cannot choose an omit field. Verification recomputes that identity and refuses
   140	unsupported or malformed schema contracts, a missing or malformed selected
   141	self field, raw-byte `chunk_id` objects, mutable journal variants,
   142	self-included digests, duplicate keys, unsafe integers, and floating-point
   143	literals.
   144	
   145	This package is read-only and deterministic; it does not mutate durable state.
   146	It supplies identity calculation for a new schema-versioned object under
   147	Section 17.3, but does not claim to implement migration publication, atomic
   148	reference advancement, rollback retention, `ax migrate`, `ax doctor`, or any
   149	runtime capability. Those surfaces remain unavailable until their owning
   150	implementation tasks land.
   151	
   152	Run its focused tests with:
   153	
   154	```bash
   155	go test ./internal/canonicaljson -count=1
   156	go test ./internal/canonicaljson -cover -count=1
   157	```
