 11342	### 16.7 Directory, enrichment, query, and terminal safety
 11343	
 11344	Directory inputs include hostile transcript/tool text, repository/provider
 11345	names, paths, model output, peer records, query strings, and terminal text. No
 11346	content obtained from a session is an instruction to an adapter, worker,
 11347	planner, shell, terminal, or operator action. Synthetic prompts/checkpoints are
 11348	constructed from typed escaped fields; arbitrary summaries never select tools,
 11349	paths, schema tags, permissions, routes, or argv.
 11350	
 11351	Discovery reads only allowlisted adapter-declared native roots and explicitly
 11352	rejects credential/auth roots. Raw native IDs, transcript/preview bodies,
 11353	system/developer instructions, hidden/opaque reasoning, raw tools, attachments,
 11354	files, credentials, auth databases, environment values, model payloads,
 11355	terminal output, PIDs, PTYs, sockets, and absolute native-store paths are
 11356	excluded from directory replication, default indexing, plans, logs, and
 11357	metrics. Authentication is only the four-value status enum.
 11358	
 11359	Enrichment inputs are immutable, bounded, redacted public user/assistant
 11360	projections by default. The worker has no ambient filesystem, shell, network,
 11361	provider, Session, lease, workspace-write, terminal, or cloning authority.
 11362	Only an explicit Profile may grant one configured model channel; credentials
 11363	remain outside the Profile/request/receipt. Output validates the closed
 11364	annotation payload, size, evidence, head, and redaction policy before
 11365	publication and cannot set identity, ownership, capabilities, routes,
 11366	operator-only metadata, or executable arguments.
 11367	
 11368	Field authorization and redaction occur server-side before query serialization
 11369	or mesh publication; caller projection cannot widen authority. Preview and
 11370	transcript grep are source-local, explicit, and hard-bounded. Metadata policy
 11371	tightening prevents new sends but is not a remote deletion claim. Debug native-
 11372	file logging is off by default, local, bounded, owner-only, and requires a
 11373	redacted export manifest.
 11374	
 11375	All native/process launches use structured argv, explicit workspace-derived cwd,
 11376	minimal environment allowlists, safe-open/no-follow path handling, owner-only
 11377	staging, and existing cloning/provider transaction authorities. Provider IDs,
 11378	titles, paths, queries, and transcript fragments are never evaluated by a
 11379	shell. TUI and CLI rendering strips or visibly escapes ANSI/OSC sequences,
 11380	control characters, bidi overrides, invalid encodings, and hostile-width
 11381	graphemes before terminal output.
 11382	
 11383	Metric labels are bounded and never contain Session/instance IDs, transcript,
 11384	path, prompt, title, summary, or model input. Audit may contain plan/operation/
 11385	record IDs, actor, semantic intent, host/environment identities, policy
 11386	decision, state transition, and redacted error; it contains no content bodies,
