 11389	## 17. Compatibility and migration
 11390	
 11391	### 17.1 Semantic-version rules
 11392	
 11393	Each contract in Section 1.5 versions independently:
 11394	
 11395	- a major increment MAY break syntax or semantics and MUST require explicit
 11396	  negotiation/migration;
 11397	- a minor increment MAY add optional operations, enum values, or namespaced
 11398	  extension fields but MUST preserve all prior semantics;
 11399	- a patch increment MAY clarify constraints or fix a validator defect without
 11400	  adding a field or changing behavior.
 11401	
 11402	Specification package v0.5.0 is a minor release over v0.4.3 because it adds the
 11403	first-class TerminalBackend family and new independently versioned containing
 11404	contracts. Published v0.4.3 remains the exact immutable terminal-realm
 11405	baseline. It was a patch release over v0.4.2 that reconciled the
 11406	already approved roadmap, ownership/continuation semantics, complete Git
 11407	closure, and macOS execution-realm safety without adding or changing any
 11408	independently consumed wire member. Every contract active in v0.4.2 remained
 11409	unchanged in v0.4.3, including Structured Error 1.2.0; that release uses
 11410	existing codes with typed details. The independently versioned additions and
 11411	increments in v0.5.0 are exactly the Section 1.5 delta. Existing
 11412	v0.4.3, v0.4.2, and earlier tags remain immutable.
 11413	
 11414	Within any negotiated major version, new object data MUST live under a namespaced
 11415	<code>extensions</code> entry unless the consumer negotiated a newer minor
 11416	schema. Unknown top-level fields remain an error. Protocol peers choose the
 11417	highest mutually supported minor within a common major; they MUST NOT select a
 11418	major by coercion.
 11419	
 11420	Independent release versions do not override an explicit embedding rule.
 11421	Provider protocol and Mesh RPC major 2 and task-board bridge major 1 each bind
 11422	Structured Error 1.0.0 as Section 15.1 specifies. Provider Protocol 3, Mesh RPC
 11423	4, Terminal Backend Protocol 1, and CLI Result 4 bind Structured Error 1.3.0;
 11424	Directory/CLI/RPC 3 bindings to Error 1.2 remain exact. None negotiates the
 11425	error schema separately. Compatibility is evaluated first for the containing
 11426	protocol and then against its fixed embedded-error validator.
 11427	
 11428	The v0.2.0 correction is an explicit major-version boundary. Provider protocol
 11429	1.0.0, Mesh RPC 1.0.0, and Materialization recovery state 1.0.0 remain the
 11430	immutable v0.1.0 contracts and MUST NOT be interpreted using the corrected
 11431	2.0.0 request or journal shapes. There is no in-place migration of a live
 11432	machine-local 1.0.0 materialization transaction: upgrade MUST first reach a
 11433	safe terminal state or roll it back with the v0.1.0 implementation, then create
 11434	a new 2.0.0 transaction. A 2.0.0 peer or plugin rejects major 1 rather than
 11435	coercing its missing IDs or freezing an evolving status read.
 11436	
 11437	### 17.2 Reader/writer behavior
 11438	
 11439	A writer emits exactly the negotiated version. A reader:
 11440	
 11441	1. rejects an unsupported major;
 11442	2. accepts the same/lower supported minor;
 11443	3. preserves unknown namespaced extensions byte-for-byte when forwarding an
 11444	   immutable object;
 11445	4. rejects an unknown ownership/security enum that would affect behavior; and
 11446	5. MAY retain an unknown event as inert history but MUST NOT derive state from
 11447	   it.
 11448	
 11449	An <code>enabled = true</code> capability is valid only for the exact negotiated
 11450	contract and provider tuple or, for TerminalBackend capabilities, the exact
 11451	backend ID/implementation/protocol/generation/platform/OS evidence binding.
 11452	Version or binding mismatch changes it to conditional/unsupported and prevents
 11453	dependent activation.
 11454	
 11455	### 17.3 Immutable data migration
 11456	
 11457	Immutable objects MUST never be edited in place. A migration creates a new
 11458	schema-versioned object that references the prior object in
 11459	<code>extensions["works.relux.ax.migrated-from"]</code>. That extension value is
 11460	a closed object containing exactly <code>schema_id:string</code>,
 11461	<code>schema_version:semver</code>, and <code>object_id:digest</code>. The writer
 11462	validates the new object and atomically advances a local reference. Old objects
 11463	remain available for rollback until retention policy allows collection.
 11464	
 11465	Configuration migration MUST create a backup, write a new file atomically, and
 11466	require <code>ax migrate config</code> for a major change. The CLI MUST NOT
 11467	silently rewrite a major-version config at startup.
 11468	
 11469	The derived SQLite index MAY be rebuilt at any time. It is never a migration
 11470	source of truth.
 11471	
 11472	### 17.4 Upgrade and downgrade
 11473	
 11474	Before upgrading, <code>ax</code> SHOULD checkpoint locally owned sessions.
 11475	After upgrade it MUST run schema/plugin/task-board compatibility checks before
 11476	auto-resume.
 11477	
 11478	A downgraded binary that cannot understand current records MUST enter
 11479	read-only diagnostic mode for those sessions. It MUST NOT resume, transfer
 11480	ownership, materialize, or write lower-version replacements.
 11481	
 11482	Provider upgrades invalidate prior tuple-specific acceptance until the adapter's
 11483	declared version range and compatibility fixture cover the new version. Muse
 11484	and Antigravity unknowns in Section 8 remain explicit version gates.
 11485	
 11486	TerminalBackend upgrade negotiates Manifest, Probe, Protocol, Provider,
 11487	Configuration, Event, CLI Result, and Error versions independently. A peer that
 11488	cannot activate the backend contract MAY still browse and synchronize sanitized
 11489	immutable evidence; it MUST report activation unavailable rather than omit the
 11490	Session. Restore binds the previously selected backend and generation, while a
 11491	new owner activation may select another admitted backend. Downgrade is read-only
 11492	for every unrepresentable binding or ID and never emits a lower-version
 11493	replacement.
 11494	
 11495	### 17.5 Directory release compatibility
 11496	
 11497	AX/spec v0.4.0 introduced Directory Node/records/query at 1.0.0, Mesh RPC 3.0.0,
 11498	Configuration 2.0.0, CLI Result 3.0.0, Session Record/Event 3.0.0, and
 11499	Structured Error 1.2.0. Observation Event remains 1.0.0 because its event name
 11500	is an open grammar and its object shape is unchanged. Provider Protocol remains
