   284	code units as required by RFC 8785 Section 3.2.3. An implementation whose native
   285	string ordering uses Unicode scalar values, UTF-8 bytes, locale collation, or
   286	another ordering MUST explicitly derive the UTF-16 ordering before hashing.
   287	The common logical data model forbids floating-point values, so the remaining
   288	JCS number surface is limited to the safe integers defined below. Decoders MUST
   289	reject lone surrogate code points before canonicalization.
