   935	
   936	The generation digest uses SHA-256 over UTF-8
   937	<code>ax-terminal-backend-generation-v1\0</code> followed by the backend's
   938	host-local raw generation bytes; it neither reveals nor reconstructs that
   939	generation. Manifest-to-Probe reconciliation is the following closed rule. The
   940	Probe <code>terminal_backend_id</code>, <code>implementation_version</code>,
   941	<code>implementation_kind</code>, and <code>executable_digest</code> MUST equal
   942	the Manifest members; its <code>protocol_version</code> MUST be exactly one member
   943	of <code>protocol_versions</code>, and its <code>platform</code> MUST be exactly
   944	one member of <code>platforms</code>. Array-to-scalar selection is membership,
   945	not aggregate equality.
   946	
   947	Let <code>M[c]</code> be the one Manifest static claim for capability
   948	<code>c</code>, when present, and <code>P[c]</code> the one Probe claim. The
   949	declared sorted-unique constraints make a duplicate key invalid before this
   950	reconciliation runs. The complete keyed relation is:
   951	
   952	1. Every <code>M[c]</code> MUST have exactly one <code>P[c]</code>; omission is a
   953	   manifest/probe mismatch.
   954	2. <code>P[c].origin=static</code> is permitted only when <code>M[c]</code>
   955	   exists, and <code>P[c]</code> MUST then equal <code>M[c]</code> member for
   956	   member. It is a static echo, not a new observation.
   957	3. <code>P[c].origin=probed</code> with an existing <code>M[c]</code> is a
   958	   generation-bound override. It is permitted only when
   959	   <code>M[c].generation_variable=true</code>; its <code>value</code> MAY differ,
   960	   while <code>generation_variable</code>, <code>dependent_operations</code>, and
   961	   <code>evidence_requirements</code> MUST remain equal to <code>M[c]</code> and
   962	   the capability registry row.
   963	4. <code>P[c].origin=probed</code> without <code>M[c]</code> is a probed
   964	   addition. It is permitted only for a capability in the closed registry, and
   965	   its three registry-derived members MUST equal that row. A Probe cannot add
   966	   a claim with <code>origin=static</code>.
   967	5. A true <code>P[c]</code> is admitted only when unexpired Capability Evidence
   968	   bound to this exact Manifest/Probe tuple satisfies every listed evidence
   969	   requirement. The required fact mapping is
   970	   <code>conformance_fixture-&gt;fixture_passed</code>,
   971	   <code>runtime_probe-&gt;runtime_probe_passed</code>,
   972	   <code>credential_sentinel-&gt;sentinel_passed</code>,
   973	   <code>provider_auth_smoke-&gt;provider_auth_passed</code>, and
   974	   <code>policy_authorization-&gt;policy_checked</code>. A false claim has no
   975	   matching Capability Evidence because Evidence <code>value</code> is the
   976	   literal <code>true</code>.
   977	6. <code>evidence_ids</code> MUST be exactly the sorted unique IDs of all
   978	   returned Capability Evidence objects used by true <code>P</code> claims.
   979	   Every referenced object MUST name exactly one present true claim; an ID for
   980	   an absent or false claim, an unreferenced returned object, conflicting
   981	   evidence, or duplicate/conflicting claims invalidates the whole Probe.
   982	
   983	A partial, malformed, stale, or failed Manifest, Probe, or evidence read is an
   984	error, never absence or availability. Any failed equality, membership, keyed
   985	relation, evidence binding, or evidence coverage rule is
   986	<code>terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch</code> and fails before
   987	activation; executable substitution or implementation drift additionally maps
   988	to its more specific Section 15.3 code.
   989	
   990	Discovery completes before activation. Duplicate/ambiguous IDs,
   991	manifest/probe disagreement, implementation drift, untrusted executable
   992	substitution, stale generation, unknown identity/version, or unevidenced claims
   993	fail closed. A manifest is not availability proof. External adapters use argv
   994	and local length-prefixed framing: unsigned 32-bit big-endian byte length plus
   995	UTF-8 JSON, at most 1 MiB, one request/response at a time. EOF, oversize,
   996	invalid JSON, unsolicited output, or deadline expiry terminates the adapter.
   997	M0 exposes only an internal semantic interface and conformance harness; a
   998	stable public SDK is deferred until tmux and one materially different backend
   999	validate the boundary.
  1000	
  1001	Manifest, Probe, Binding, and Capability Evidence IDs equal the lowercase
  1002	<code>sha256:</code> digest of RFC 8785 JCS bytes with their own ID member
  1003	omitted. A reader MUST recompute the ID before use. Manifest and Probe remain
  1004	immutable observations when later probes supersede them.
