 11455	### 17.3 Immutable data migration
 11456	
 11457	Immutable objects MUST never be edited in place. A migration creates a new
 11458	schema-versioned object that references the prior object in
 11459	<code>extensions["works.relux.ax.migrated-from"]</code>. That extension value is
 11460	a closed object containing exactly <code>schema_id:string</code>,
 11461	<code>schema_version:semver</code>, and <code>object_id:digest</code>. The writer
 11462	validates the new object and atomically advances a local reference. Old objects
 11463	remain available for rollback until retention policy allows collection.

